Third-party code in dashboard/
==============================

CSR (https://github.com/archelium/csr), commit ba6dad0, file sc_livelog.py, is used under the
MIT License below. Code adapted from it is marked "From CSR" where it sits, with what was changed:

- dashboard/scdash/events.py
    line patterns: the notice and its id (sc_livelog.py lines 16 and 45), the notice's mission
    and objective ids (36), the quantum target (51), the route's fuel estimate (52), the login
    handle (33), the location inventory (29), the destroyed vehicle (20-23), <EndMission> (35),
    and, in the notice kinds table, the contract notices (17), the objective notices (53), the
    jurisdiction notice (18), the armistice notices (395-400), the blueprint notice (28) and the
    injury notice (19); the notice-cleaning helper `clean` (84-90, here `notice_text` and
    MARKUP_RE) and `real_mid` (117-119, here `real_mission`).
- dashboard/scdash/records.py
    the closing-quote test of a HUD notice (line 46), the waiting for a notice's pieces (248-252)
    and the joining of its continuation pieces (173-182).
- dashboard/scdash/state.py
    from LogState (lines 128-434): the place history (199-204), the quantum target and route
    (219-232), <EndMission> (241-247), _contract_for (296-299), _objective (301-324) and the
    contract notices (405-425).
- dashboard/scdash/tail.py
    from LiveTail.poll (lines 448-467): a file shorter than the offset is a new log (454), and
    the unfinished last line is kept for the next read (462-465).
- dashboard/scdash/telemetry.py
    from CSR's sc_telemetry.py (same commit, same license): the reader's retry-and-silence
    loop follows Recorder (lines 754-946: the game_running callable, 769; stop() closing the
    open stream from the calling thread, 804-815; the refusal timing in _cycle, 887-946; the
    silence check in _read, 985-999) and its timings (699-707), rewritten; the capture file's
    name from its UTC start, made unique when taken, and its started_utc key follow
    Recorder._open_file (964-977); a cut-off capture keeps what came before, as
    read_recording does (653-671), the idea only; the time-and-length records follow the raw
    fixtures CSR's tests read (tests/tlm_helpers.py lines 159-169, read_raw), the idea only.
    From CSR's sc_stats.py: the startup block's 1,500 lines and the service's log marker
    (lines 1449-1452).
- dashboard/scdash/telemetry_h2.py
    from CSR's sc_telemetry.py lines 325-450: the frame types and flags (325-327), _frame
    (330-331), _hpack_int (334-344), _hpack_str (347-349), _request_headers (352-360) and
    GrpcStream (363-450). Changed: host and request block fixed and checked at the one write,
    every size and rate capped, a bounded flow-control window, a private socket, a connect
    another thread can end, poll() for messages(), only status codes kept from the server.
- dashboard/scdash/telemetry_proto.py
    from CSR's sc_telemetry.py lines 1-320: _varint (33-41) and wire_fields (44-61), bounded;
    the field type numbers (66-73); descriptor_blobs (85-116), read in pieces with full
    sharing; Schema (119-283), with presence, bounds and unknown fields kept, and its dump
    (210-222) as describe(); load_schema (286-320), with a cache rebuilt from the descriptor
    bytes it holds, scans held off while the program file may be changing, and no exceptions.
- dashboard/scdash/telemetry_readings.py
    from CSR's sc_telemetry.py: FLOAT_SENTINEL (455), flatten (486-505) and frame_events
    (508-510); and, as rules in its table, the field quirks in CSR's docs/telemetry/NOTES.md
    and the reading of ifcs_coupled.active in CSR's sc_slate.py (line 2822).
- dashboard/tests/test_telemetry.py
    from CSR's tests: wait_for (tests/test_tlm_recorder.py lines 18-24), and the ideas of the
    tests for start after stop (396-406), no schema (183-194), idle with the game not running
    (208-219), a loop that survives errors (220-238) and silent streams (239-272).
- dashboard/tests/test_telemetry_fake.py
    from CSR's tests/tlm_helpers.py: enc_varint (16-27, unchanged, here vint), enc_field
    (30-37, split into key, ld and vi), the descriptor builders _field, _msg, _enum and _file
    (53-84) and the service built in make_descriptor (136-138), the gRPC message prefix and
    response and trailer blocks (212-219, 298), free_port (237-242, unchanged), and
    StreamServer's one plan per connection with the last repeating (245-311); the frame
    helper is sc_telemetry.py's _frame (330-331); the snapshot builder follows actor_frame
    (227-234), the idea only.
- dashboard/tests/test_telemetry_proto.py
    from CSR's tests: the ideas of the decoder and loader tests in tests/test_tlm_core.py
    (DecodeTests 26-59, the opener spy 78-104, LoadSchemaTests 124-148) and of the synthetic
    program file in tests/tlm_helpers.py (exe_bytes, 172-177).
- dashboard/tests/test_telemetry_readings.py
    from CSR's tests/test_tlm_recording.py: the ideas of the flatten and frame_events tests
    (24-43).

No code from any project other than CSR is used in dashboard/.


